enchilada: display + reboot: no frame waits at shutdown, halt hook restores ABL's scanout, bounded reset

Boots 26/27 (sweetzc=1): `launchctl reboot` ended in "Halt/Restart Timed Out" 30 s into
PEHaltRestart, and after boot 27 the panic reset did not come either; boot 28 (no sweetzc) read PON
subtype 0 once at 13.1 s and had reboot-to-fastboot off for the whole boot.
Display: shutdown, restart and panic restart now reach SweetFramebuffer through
SweetPlatformExpert's PE_halt_restart (sweet_fb_halt, before sweet_reboot_fastboot) and, earlier,
through a priority sleep/wake interest (kIOMessageSystemWillRestart/PowerOff). That path takes no
lock and waits for no frame: flips stop for good, the pool closes, ABL's registers are written back
if a flip moved the pipe (idempotent stores, as the panic hook), and the console draws again so the
restart's own lines are on the panel. System sleep pauses flips until wake. Display off (vsync
tick, try-lock) only issues the restore; the held surface is let go once a later tick sees the
flush taken. The 50 ms wait remains only in SwapEnd, and gives up as soon as shutdown or sleep
starts.
Reboot (0200): PON subtype/spare are read up to 5 times 10 ms apart (keys thread held each time,
failed tries logged with the transfer status), and once more at the first restart if all failed.
A panic after a restart that already marked the spare goes straight to the reset, no SPMI round
trip. The reset is PSCI SYSTEM_RESET, entered at most once (a CPU that never came back may hold the
secure side, so a later panic does not issue another SMC), then PS_HOLD = 0 if, and only if, the
PMIC's PS_HOLD reset is enabled as a warm reset (read at boot: SOFT_RB_SPARE and IMEM survive that,
a hard reset could boot Android). Every wait is bounded; nothing waits on another CPU's flag.

